config MQ_IOSCHED_FLOW
	tristate "Multi-Lane I/O scheduler (FLOW)"
	default m
	help
	  The Multi-Lane I/O scheduler (FLOW) v3.1 LSB is a blk-mq I/O
	  scheduler with three priority tiers (Emergency > Read > Write),
	  deadline-sorted rbtree dispatch, and a generalised N-lane
	  starvation-bound framework (starvation_max_read / starvation_max_write)
	  that is provably starvation-free by construction.

	  Lane-Starvation Bounding (LSB) refactor:
	    - Formal starvation-bound dispatch with per-lane max_bypass/
	      bypass_count counters (generalises mq-deadline to N lanes)
	    - No autotune timer (static parameters, like mq-deadline)
	    - No per-process scheduling state
	    - ~700 lines, auditable in a single sitting

	  Removed in v3.1:
	    - Per-process budget containment (caused permanent write starvation
	      under sequential write loads — the budget refill formula
	      sectors/100 returned 0 for all I/Os < 50 KB, and the 100ms idle
	      safety valve never fired during continuous writes)
	    - 3-mode autotune timer (unproven benefit; mq-deadline uses static
	      parameters and works correctly across all workloads)
	    - Per-ICQ state (last_io_completed was not read by scheduling path)

config MQ_IOSCHED_DEFAULT_FLOW
	bool "Enable FLOW I/O scheduler as the default MQ scheduler"
	depends on MQ_IOSCHED_FLOW
	help
	  Make flow-iosched the default MQ I/O scheduler.  Note: this
	  requires wiring into elevator_set_default() in block/elevator.c,
	  which is kernel-version-specific and is NOT handled by this
	  patch.  For most users, the standalone module install script
	  (install-flow-iosched.sh) is the recommended approach.
